    "summary": "Email from cs@core.cn impersonates Microsoft 365 support, urging login within 24 hours to complete account verification or lose Outlook/Teams/OneDrive access. The sole link, https://sakura-cat3.com/, is unrelated to Microsoft and serves a SakuraCat VPN login page collecting Email/Password credentials — a clear brand conflict with the email narrative. Two earlier identical messages from the same sender (mail_log_id 3 and 6) form a small campaign; the sender first appeared today and SPF/DKIM/DMARC are all absent. Threat intel and RBL show no hits and the domain is 615 days old, which slightly tempers certainty, but the impersonation, credential-collection landing page, and campaign pattern support phishing.",
